If a patient has a pain and the patient has a single-joint-osteoarthritis and a nonpharmacologic-intervention does not improve the pain then it is possible that a topical-NSAID treats the pain.
If a patient has a pain and the patient has a few-joint-osteoarthritis and a nonpharmacologic-intervention does not improve the pain then it is possible that a topical-NSAID treats the pain.
